{"availability":"available","full":"lokutor-ai/ito","name":"ito","description":"Natural-sounding streaming text-to-speech for the ESP32-S3: 4.4 M params, 4.9 MB, no cloud, no NPU","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"C","stars":16,"forks":1,"created":"2026-10-02T14:45:34Z","updated":"2026-10-05T18:04:19Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://lokutor-ai.github.io/ito/","topics":["edge-ai","embedded","esp32","esp32-s3","microcontroller","speech-synthesis","streaming","text-to-speech","tinyml","tts"],"demo":"https://lokutor-ai.github.io/ito/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T20:09:09.086Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T20:09:09.086Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T20:09:09.086Z","lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","discoveredVia":[],"metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T08:24:09.857Z","stars":2,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-04T10:32:23.845Z","stars":5,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-06T16:31:26.142Z","stars":11,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-08T20:09:09.086Z","stars":16,"forks":1}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Ito is English text-to-speech that runs entirely on an ESP32-S3 (240 MHz dual-core Xtensa LX7, 8 MB PSRAM, 16 MB flash), with no cloud and no neural accelerator. It streams: audio starts after a short first chunk (125 ms) is ready, and the work before it does not grow with the sentence length. The voice is distilled from a large open TTS model into 3.3 M parameters. Built by Lokutor, the makers of Oído (speech recognition on the same chip).","Status (5 October 2026). The on-chip engine is verified on a laptop and in Espressif's QEMU emulator: the firmware's audio is bit-identical to the host build of the engine, and every sample in samples/ is that engine's exact output. Nothing has run on a physical board yet. Time to first audio and real-time factor are estimated from exact instruction counts (QEMU) and an assumed PSRAM bandwidth. Real-time playback is not established on silicon: with the main weight set the optimistic and central estimates are faster than real time (RTF 0.43–0.47 and 0.63–0.66) and the pessimistic one is only…","Licensing in one line. The code is GPLv3; the voice model that makes it talk is non-commercial (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 + terms). Hobby, research and education use is welcome. For anything commercial, or if you are a small team that wants to build with it, talk to us: we like collaborating."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lokutor-ai/ito/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"c414035e560cfa9b4450bdd0677f8876a295aa6743d9ee682418d65d5f09bc9b","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T16:35:34.988Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T16:35:34.988Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Ito is English text-to-speech that runs entirely on an ESP32-S3 (240 MHz dual-core Xtensa LX7, 8 MB PSRAM, 16 MB flash), with no cloud and no neural accelerator. It streams: audio starts after a short first chunk (125 ms) is ready, and the work before it does not grow with the sentence length. The voice is distilled from a large open TTS model into 3.3 M parameters. Built by Lokutor, the makers of Oído (speech recognition on the same chip).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lokutor-ai/ito/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Open it, accept the terms (free for research, education and personal projects), then log in on your machine:","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lokutor-ai/ito/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"c414035e560cfa9b4450bdd0677f8876a295aa6743d9ee682418d65d5f09bc9b","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lokutor-ai/ito/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T16:35:34.988Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-05T18:04:19Z","overviewAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T16:35:28.877Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/lokutor-ai/ito/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T16:35:34.989Z","hash":"c414035e560cfa9b4450bdd0677f8876a295aa